{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01WNJ7o5MisviRohhUnx9fXu","type":"tool_result","content":"\"\"\"Which of the `better_move` fix's two changes carries its cost? (plan 3 §1\nQ1a, loop0004 item 04)\n\nThe 2026-09-26 fix of the C `better_move` (`0eb33915`, `reports/better_move_bug.md`\n§7) changed the rule in two places: the close count `close(q, S ∪ {r})` no\nlonger counts customers `r` finishes on its own, and the subset rule now runs\n*before* better move so that no rule cites a candidate another has discarded.\nThe fixed rule costs +7.3% nodes at n ≤ 40, ×2–3.5 on the 100-customer\nhalf-ratio classes and ≥ 15× on `Random-100-100-2-4_0` (§18). This module\ntoggles the two changes separately, behind flags that default to today's rule\n(`old_close_count`, `old_rule_order` on `satisfiability.customer_search.decide`,\nbits of `better_move_variant` on the C's new entry point `cs_decide_variant`),\nand measures four variants:\n\n    fixed      today's rule (both corrections)\n    old-close  the over-counting close count, today's rule order\n    old-order  today's close count, better move before the subset rule\n    prefix     both reverted: the rule as it stood before the fix\n\nand one candidate that is not a revert, added once the four had been\nmeasured: `bm-first`, better move first over every candidate, then the\nsubset rule over its survivors citing nothing better move discarded -- the\npre-fix order with the cycle closed off, `BM_SUBSET_RESTRICTED` in the C.\n\nTwo stages, then tables:\n\n- `harness`: every certified instance at n ≤ 40 on which Theorem 2 is\n  switched on (`sparse_enough_for_better_move`), the identity, eight\n  relabellings and one re-covering (`learning.differential.labellings`),\n  `decide(optimum − 1)` and `decide(optimum)` under each variant, `csearch`\n  configuration (`better_move_dominators = 0`). A `sat` below the optimum or\n  an `unsat` at it is a false answer; the pre-fix variant must reproduce §15's\n  56 instances / 88 false answers or the reproduction is wrong.\n- `scale`: identity labelling, `decide(optimum − 1)` only, each variant, on\n  the campaign at 50–100 (`results_upward.csv`), the corpus at 41–100 where\n  Theorem 2 is on, and `Random-100-100-2-4_0` at a 600 s deadline. A censored\n  call is a lower bound on nodes, never a missing value.\n\nNothing here decides `k` for anything: the flags are unsound by construction\nand exist to be measured. Nothing is written to `solutions/`.\n\nRun:\n\n    python -m learning.fix_cost --stage harness --workers 14\n    python -m learning.fix_cost --stage scale --workers 14 --deadline 60 --corpus-deadline 120\n    python -m learning.fix_cost --stage tables\n\nWrites `learning/data/ensemble/fix_cost_harness.csv.gz`,\n`learning/data/ensemble/fix_cost_scale.csv` (both appended as jobs finish; a\nrerun of `scale` skips pairs already present) and `reports/fix_cost_tables.md`.\n\"\"\"\n\nfrom __future__ import annotations\n\nimport argparse\nimport multiprocessing as mp\nimport time\nfrom pathlib import Path\n\nimport numpy as np\nimport pandas as pd\n\nfrom learning.differential import (\n    DEFAULT_INSTANCE_DIR,\n    DEFAULT_SOLUTIONS_DIR,\n    ENSEMBLE_DIR,\n    RELABELLINGS,\n    RESULTS_CSV,\n    _materialise,\n    campaign_targets,\n    corpus_targets,\n    labellings,\n    witness_value,\n)\nfrom mosp.instance import MOSPInstance\n\nVARIANTS: dict[str, dict[str, bool]] = {\n    \"fixed\": {},\n    \"old-close\": {\"old_close_count\": True},\n    \"old-order\": {\"old_rule_order\": True},\n55:import argparse\n107:def decide_variant(instance: MOSPInstance, k: int, variant: str,\n128:def false_answers(row: dict) -> int:\n143:def harness_targets(max_customers: int = 40, limit: int | None = None,\n153:def harness_rows(instance: MOSPInstance, optimum: int, relabellings: int = RELABELLINGS,\n183:def _harness_job(args) -> list[dict]:\n192:def run_harness(jobs: list[dict], workers: int = 14, relabellings: int = RELABELLINGS,\n207:    def _flush() -> None:\n213:    def _consume(rows: list[dict]) -> None:\n250:def scale_targets(upward_csv: Path = UPWARD_CSV, min_customers: int = 41,\n284:def _scale_job(args) -> dict:\n298:def run_scale(jobs: list[dict], workers: int = 14, out: Path = SCALE_CSV,\n315:    def _flush() -> None:\n344:def _band(n: int) -> str:\n351:def _md(frame: pd.DataFrame, floatfmt: str = \".3g\") -> str:\n357:def soundness_table(rows: pd.DataFrame) -> pd.DataFrame:\n380:def _paired(rows: pd.DataFrame, value: str = \"nodes_lo\", status: str = \"status_lo\",\n392:def ratio_summary(wide: pd.DataFrame, num: str, den: str) -> dict:\n412:def attribution_table(wide: pd.DataFrame) -> pd.DataFrame:\n417:def attribution_by_group(wide: pd.DataFrame, group: pd.Series) -> pd.DataFrame:\n433:def totals_table(wide: pd.DataFrame) -> pd.DataFrame:\n440:def scale_status_table(scale: pd.DataFrame) -> pd.DataFrame:\n455:def scale_censored_bounds(scale: pd.DataFrame) -> pd.DataFrame:\n473:def reproduction_table(scale: pd.DataFrame) -> pd.DataFrame:\n487:def write_tables(harness_csv: Path = HARNESS_CSV, scale_csv: Path = SCALE_CSV,\n573:def main() -> None:\n574:    ap = argparse.ArgumentParser(description=__doc__.split(\"\\n\")[0])\n575:    ap.add_argument(\"--stage\", choices=(\"harness\", \"scale\", \"tables\"), default=\"tables\")\n576:    ap.add_argument(\"--workers\", type=int, default=14)\n577:    ap.add_argument(\"--source\", choices=(\"all\", \"campaign\", \"corpus\"), default=\"all\")\n578:    ap.add_argument(\"--limit\", type=int, default=None)\n579:    ap.add_argument(\"--max-customers\", type=int, default=40)\n580:    ap.add_argument(\"--relabellings\", type=int, default=RELABELLINGS)\n581:    ap.add_argument(\"--deadline\", type=float, default=60.0, help=\"seconds per call\")\n582:    ap.add_argument(\"--corpus-deadline\", type=float, default=120.0,\n584:    ap.add_argument(\"--min-customers\", type=int, default=41, help=\"scale stage lower size\")\n585:    ap.add_argument(\"--scale-max\", type=int, default=100)\n586:    ap.add_argument(\"--wall\", type=float, default=None, help=\"stop dispatching after this many seconds\")\n587:    ap.add_argument(\"--harness-csv\", type=Path, default=HARNESS_CSV)\n588:    ap.add_argument(\"--scale-csv\", type=Path, default=SCALE_CSV)\n589:    ap.add_argument(\"--variants\", nargs=\"*\", default=list(VARIANT_ORDER),\n591:    ap.add_argument(\"--out\", type=Path, default=TABLES)","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"25acc2df-f9dd-4945-9455-4c38c02b4b56","uuid":"a8c0825b-2af5-4112-8859-58134829a608","timestamp":"2026-10-01T14:54:04.451Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"\"\"\"Which of the `better_move` fix's two changes carries its cost? (plan 3 §1\nQ1a, loop0004 item 04)\n\nThe 2026-09-26 fix of the C `better_move` (`0eb33915`, `reports/better_move_bug.md`\n§7) changed the rule in two places: the close count `close(q, S ∪ {r})` no\nlonger counts customers `r` finishes on its own, and the subset rule now runs\n*before* better move so that no rule cites a candidate another has discarded.\nThe fixed rule costs +7.3% nodes at n ≤ 40, ×2–3.5 on the 100-customer\nhalf-ratio classes and ≥ 15× on `Random-100-100-2-4_0` (§18). This module\ntoggles the two changes separately, behind flags that default to today's rule\n(`old_close_count`, `old_rule_order` on `satisfiability.customer_search.decide`,\nbits of `better_move_variant` on the C's new entry point `cs_decide_variant`),\nand measures four variants:\n\n    fixed      today's rule (both corrections)\n    old-close  the over-counting close count, today's rule order\n    old-order  today's close count, better move before the subset rule\n    prefix     both reverted: the rule as it stood before the fix\n\nand one candidate that is not a revert, added once the four had been\nmeasured: `bm-first`, better move first over every candidate, then the\nsubset rule over its survivors citing nothing better move discarded -- the\npre-fix order with the cycle closed off, `BM_SUBSET_RESTRICTED` in the C.\n\nTwo stages, then tables:\n\n- `harness`: every certified instance at n ≤ 40 on which Theorem 2 is\n  switched on (`sparse_enough_for_better_move`), the identity, eight\n  relabellings and one re-covering (`learning.differential.labellings`),\n  `decide(optimum − 1)` and `decide(optimum)` under each variant, `csearch`\n  configuration (`better_move_dominators = 0`). A `sat` below the optimum or\n  an `unsat` at it is a false answer; the pre-fix variant must reproduce §15's\n  56 instances / 88 false answers or the reproduction is wrong.\n- `scale`: identity labelling, `decide(optimum − 1)` only, each variant, on\n  the campaign at 50–100 (`results_upward.csv`), the corpus at 41–100 where\n  Theorem 2 is on, and `Random-100-100-2-4_0` at a 600 s deadline. A censored\n  call is a lower bound on nodes, never a missing value.\n\nNothing here decides `k` for anything: the flags are unsound by construction\nand exist to be measured. Nothing is written to `solutions/`.\n\nRun:\n\n    python -m learning.fix_cost --stage harness --workers 14\n    python -m learning.fix_cost --stage scale --workers 14 --deadline 60 --corpus-deadline 120\n    python -m learning.fix_cost --stage tables\n\nWrites `learning/data/ensemble/fix_cost_harness.csv.gz`,\n`learning/data/ensemble/fix_cost_scale.csv` (both appended as jobs finish; a\nrerun of `scale` skips pairs already present) and `reports/fix_cost_tables.md`.\n\"\"\"\n\nfrom __future__ import annotations\n\nimport argparse\nimport multiprocessing as mp\nimport time\nfrom pathlib import Path\n\nimport numpy as np\nimport pandas as pd\n\nfrom learning.differential import (\n    DEFAULT_INSTANCE_DIR,\n    DEFAULT_SOLUTIONS_DIR,\n    ENSEMBLE_DIR,\n    RELABELLINGS,\n    RESULTS_CSV,\n    _materialise,\n    campaign_targets,\n    corpus_targets,\n    labellings,\n    witness_value,\n)\nfrom mosp.instance import MOSPInstance\n\nVARIANTS: dict[str, dict[str, bool]] = {\n    \"fixed\": {},\n    \"old-close\": {\"old_close_count\": True},\n    \"old-order\": {\"old_rule_order\": True},\n55:import argparse\n107:def decide_variant(instance: MOSPInstance, k: int, variant: str,\n128:def false_answers(row: dict) -> int:\n143:def harness_targets(max_customers: int = 40, limit: int | None = None,\n153:def harness_rows(instance: MOSPInstance, optimum: int, relabellings: int = RELABELLINGS,\n183:def _harness_job(args) -> list[dict]:\n192:def run_harness(jobs: list[dict], workers: int = 14, relabellings: int = RELABELLINGS,\n207:    def _flush() -> None:\n213:    def _consume(rows: list[dict]) -> None:\n250:def scale_targets(upward_csv: Path = UPWARD_CSV, min_customers: int = 41,\n284:def _scale_job(args) -> dict:\n298:def run_scale(jobs: list[dict], workers: int = 14, out: Path = SCALE_CSV,\n315:    def _flush() -> None:\n344:def _band(n: int) -> str:\n351:def _md(frame: pd.DataFrame, floatfmt: str = \".3g\") -> str:\n357:def soundness_table(rows: pd.DataFrame) -> pd.DataFrame:\n380:def _paired(rows: pd.DataFrame, value: str = \"nodes_lo\", status: str = \"status_lo\",\n392:def ratio_summary(wide: pd.DataFrame, num: str, den: str) -> dict:\n412:def attribution_table(wide: pd.DataFrame) -> pd.DataFrame:\n417:def attribution_by_group(wide: pd.DataFrame, group: pd.Series) -> pd.DataFrame:\n433:def totals_table(wide: pd.DataFrame) -> pd.DataFrame:\n440:def scale_status_table(scale: pd.DataFrame) -> pd.DataFrame:\n455:def scale_censored_bounds(scale: pd.DataFrame) -> pd.DataFrame:\n473:def reproduction_table(scale: pd.DataFrame) -> pd.DataFrame:\n487:def write_tables(harness_csv: Path = HARNESS_CSV, scale_csv: Path = SCALE_CSV,\n573:def main() -> None:\n574:    ap = argparse.ArgumentParser(description=__doc__.split(\"\\n\")[0])\n575:    ap.add_argument(\"--stage\", choices=(\"harness\", \"scale\", \"tables\"), default=\"tables\")\n576:    ap.add_argument(\"--workers\", type=int, default=14)\n577:    ap.add_argument(\"--source\", choices=(\"all\", \"campaign\", \"corp